======================================================================
INTRODUCTION
============

PortConfig  is  basically  a  serial  port  configuration  program for
several  programs  written  by  me.   These  progrmas include GateTerm
outdialer, TeleVal callback verifier, and MTalk multi-user conference.
It  was written so that each of these programs can use the same serial
port   configuration   files.    Its  alleviates  the  development  of
telecommunication  programs  and  saves  the  user time from having to
configure  the  serial  port for each of my programs that accesses it.
Of  course,  if  you  don't  have  any of the mentioned programs, this
program is pretty useless.

This  document  only  explains  how  to  get  PortConfig installed and
running.   To  actually  use the program, you must read the help files
which are accessible from the help command ([H] menu-item).


======================================================================
REQUIREMENTS
============

This  program  runs  on  any Amiga(tm) with version 2.04 of the OS.  A
system  with  512K would suffice.


======================================================================
INSTALLATION
============

You  must  put PortConfig and its accompanying files into the assigned
directory  called  DOORS:ASI.   DOORS:   is the proposed directory for
doors  (or  BBS  utilities)  used  by  many  system operators and door
programmers.   ASI is a directory where you should put the BBS or comm
utilities  written  by  me.   You must also create several directories
within  DOORS:ASI.  However, when you unLHA the archive it will create
some of these directories for you.  The directories are:

DOORS:ASI/bin/        -- Where all executable files go.
DOORS:ASI/config/     -- Where all configuration files go.
DOORS:ASI/data/       -- Where all the data files go.
DOORS:ASI/doc/        -- Where all the documents go.
DOORS:ASI/help/       -- Where all the help files go.
DOORS:ASI/log/        -- Where all the log files go.
DOORS:ASI/key/        -- Where all the key files go.
DOORS:ASI/script/     -- Where all the scripts go.
DOORS:ASI/text/       -- Where all other text files go.
DOORS:ASI/user/       -- Where all the data on users go.

The files pertaining to GateTerm are as follows:

DOORS:ASI/bin/PortConfig
  -- Port Configuration program.
DOORS:ASI/config/GateTerm.PORT
  -- A sample serial port file for GateTerm, but it can be used for
     TeleVal and MTalk too.
DOORS:ASI/help/PortConfig/
  -- Online help files.

It  is  important  that  you  put  these  files  in  their  designated
directories under their original names, because other programs may try
to access them.


======================================================================
USAGE
=====

Usage: PortConfig <key> <value> ...

keys:

 COLS       display columns (default 80)
 ROWS       display rows (default 24)
 COLOR/CLR  display color? (default NO)
 CLS        clear screen where appropriate? (default NO)
 PFILE/PF   ports file to edit
            (default DOORS:ASI/config/GateTerm.PORT)

Example:
PortConfig COLS 80 ROWS 48 CLS Y PF DOORS:ASI/config/TeleVal.PORT


======================================================================
UPDATES
=======

Updates will probably be included in packages that support PortConfig.
PortConfig  will  not  likely  to  be distributed by itself, unless of
course I found a serious bug in the program.


